1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,210
Listen to a talk on a psychology podcast.

2
00:00:02,210 --> 00:00:08,150
Woman: The placebo effect occurs when people experience real health improvements after receiving a treatment

3
00:00:08,150 --> 00:00:14,090
with no medical value-like a sugar pill-simply because they believe it's real.

4
00:00:14,090 --> 00:00:22,070
Clinical trials use various placebos, including creams, gels, or even fake devices.

5
00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:26,791
It's important that these are designed to closely resemble actual treatments.

6
00:00:26,791 --> 00:00:29,620
This ensures that participants can't tell

7
00:00:29,620 --> 00:00:33,479
whether they're receiving the real treatment or the placebo,

8
00:00:33,479 --> 00:00:38,200
which in turn keeps the study fair and the results scientifically reliable.

9
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:42,948
The placebo effect highlights the powerful connection between mind and body.

10
00:00:42,948 --> 00:00:46,833
It's influenced by factors such as patient expectations,

11
00:00:46,833 --> 00:00:51,150
how the treatment is delivered, and the provider's credibility.

12
00:00:51,150 --> 00:00:55,367
In fact, a recent study found that when people expect relief,

13
00:00:55,367 --> 00:00:59,200
their brains respond as if real medicine has been given.

14
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:03,600
This expectation alone can trigger specific brain activity,

15
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:10,200
activating a pathway that links regions involved in thought, emotion, and movement.

16
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,210
When these areas work together,

17
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:14,340
they create a kind of bridge

18
00:01:14,640 --> 00:01:18,240
connecting mind and body-mental belief and physical response.

19
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:20,853
While placebos don't actually cure diseases,

20
00:01:20,853 --> 00:01:27,200
the belief that a treatment will work can lead to real improvements in how a patient feels.

21
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:30,700
So, when combined with actual medicine

22
00:01:31,300 --> 00:01:35,030
I believe this psychological boost can enhance overall care.
